# Always Use Workflows and Skills

Every change to this codebase — no matter how small — follows this workflow.

---

## Mandatory Workflow

### Step 0: Task Intake
- Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` at project root
- Identify task type (feature, bugfix, refactor, 3D/WebGL, styling, test)
- Read `.cursor/rules/` rules relevant to the task type

### Step 1: Technical Architect
- Read skill: `.cursor/skills/technical_architect/SKILL.md`
- Break down requirements: routes, components, services, NgRx (if needed), models
- Update `ARCHITECTURE.md` if structure changes
- Enforce: SOLID, standalone components, strict TS, SSR-safe, tree-shakable
- Use Angular CLI for scaffolding

### Step 2: Designer Architect
- Read skill: `.cursor/skills/designer_architect/SKILL.md`
- If Figma URL provided: call `get_design_context` via Figma MCP FIRST — no implementation until MCP responds
- Apply design tokens from `src/styles.css` `@theme` block
- Tailwind v4 only — no inline styles, no duplicate classes, no `tailwind.config.js`
- Dark mode: `dark:` prefix + CSS variables via `ThemeService` signal

### Step 3: Three.js Architect (if WebGL/canvas work)
- Read skill: `.cursor/skills/threejs-architect/SKILL.md`
- Apply to: new canvas components, shader changes, particle systems, 3D scene changes
- Enforce: SSR guard, `afterNextRender()`, cleanup/dispose, `DestroyRef`, theme reactivity via `effect()`
- Reference: `.cursor/rules/threejs-context.mdc`

### Step 4: Security
- Reference: `.cursor/rules/security-context.mdc`
- Check: XSS, static shaders, SSR safety, no `bypassSecurityTrust*` without justification
- HTTP: interceptors for tokens, validated inputs

### Step 5: Performance Monitor
- Read skill: `.cursor/skills/performance_monitor/SKILL.md`
- Angular: OnPush, signals, lazy routes, `DestroyRef` cleanup
- Three.js: capped pixel ratio, particle count ≤ 500, no object creation in RAF, full dispose
- Lighthouse ≥ 85

### Step 6: Tester
- Read skill: `.cursor/skills/tester/SKILL.md`
- Vitest 4 + jsdom — NOT Jest/Karma
- Unit tests for services, components, reducers, Three.js cleanup
- Coverage ≥ 70% — run `ng test --coverage`

### Step 7: Recheck
- Reference: `.cursor/rules/recheck_implementation.mdc`
- Run: `ng build` → zero errors
- Run: `ng test` → all pass, coverage ≥ 70%
- Verify: Figma match, dark/light mode, responsive, Three.js cleanup

